{"journal_version":1,"sequence":12,"replace_from":18,"message_count":19,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"Done. Note remaining risks: removed read-only-priority class (unstyled), priority type inline.","content":"Change made in `src/components/TaskModal.tsx`:\n\n- Replaced the read-only priority paragraph with a labelled `Priority` `<select>` (`Low` / `Medium` / `High`).\n- Added `priority` state initialized from `task.priority` and included it in the `onSave` payload alongside title and status.\n- Cancel / backdrop / Escape still just call `onCancel`, and the modal state is local, so all fields including priority are discarded; initial focus (`titleRef`) and focus restoration logic are untouched.\n- `App.tsx` and `types.ts` needed no changes: `updateTask` already replaces the whole task, so the selected-task detail picks up the new priority.\n\nCommands run (via `verify_frontend`):\n- `npm run build` (`tsc --noEmit && vite build`) — passed\n- `npm run test:public` (playwright, 6 tests) — 6 passed\n\nRemaining risks: the removed `.read-only-priority` CSS class is now unused (harmless, no styling regressions observed); the new select inherits the existing generic `label`/`select` styles rather than a dedicated class, so visual styling matches the Status control but wasn't visually inspected.","response_items":[{"id":"2d3e9c28-2117-4281-99d3-d9ab1c6e846c","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"Done. Note remaining risks: removed read-only-priority class (unstyled), priority type inline.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":"982183b6-12cc-4f92-b0cf-80863c8a4d46-0","status":"completed"},{"id":"4a120d7d-41cb-4b52-a6c1-147a6545cd42","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"Change made in `src/components/TaskModal.tsx`:\n\n- Replaced the read-only priority paragraph with a labelled `Priority` `<select>` (`Low` / `Medium` / `High`).\n- Added `priority` state initialized from `task.priority` and included it in the `onSave` payload alongs